package module // import "github.com/cymondez/pangolin-framework/kernel/module"

Package module defines module registration and lifecycle contracts, not a
runtime.

Root-mode operation scopes. The restricted lifecycle resolver deliberately
opens and closes no ephemeral scope itself, so Operation-timed services are
unreachable from module Start/Stop hooks unless the module opens an explicit
scope of its own. OpenScope turns that resolver into a module-owned di.Scope:
the underlying container scope is created here, every Resolve keeps exactly
the sealed composition's immutable module/direct-contract-owner visibility,
and Close owns the inner scope's cleanup. The root runtime, the composition
engine and the raw container are never exposed, and the owner binding is fixed
at creation.

Root Type references and optional module metadata contracts for root loading.
The loader itself lives in root_loader.go; hook interfaces and root runtime
wiring are owned by kernel/runtime and are intentionally unknown here.

Owner-private interface injection: the alias table, its Seal-driven resolution
and the guarded param resolver live here. See services.go for the composition
engine and the public contract pipeline this extends.

FUNCTIONS

func AddOperation(services Services, constructor any, opts ...AddOption) error
    AddOperation registers constructor at operation lifetime while preserving
    all existing Services.Add options such as As.

func AddSingleton(services Services, constructor any, opts ...AddOption) error
    AddSingleton registers constructor at singleton lifetime while preserving
    all existing Services.Add options such as As.

func AddTransient(services Services, constructor any, opts ...AddOption) error
    AddTransient registers constructor at transient lifetime while preserving
    all existing Services.Add options such as As.

func Contract[T any]() di.Token
    Contract returns the canonical contract token of T: a di token whose name is
    deterministically derived from the type identity.

func MustResolve[T any](ctx context.Context, resolver di.Resolver) T
    MustResolve is a panic-on-error convenience for fixtures and configuration.
    Production hooks should handle Resolve errors explicitly.

func OpenScope(ctx context.Context, resolver di.Resolver) (di.Scope, error)
    OpenScope opens one operation scope in root mode for the module
    that owns resolver: pass the restricted lifecycle resolver received
    through Runtime.Services() in a Start/Stop hook (or returned by
    Composition.LifecycleResolver(owner)). The returned di.Scope resolves
    Operation-timed services with exactly the same immutable visibility as the
    lifecycle resolver — the owner module's own registrations (including its
    owner-private interface aliases) plus direct dependencies' exported tokens —
    and never allows a different owner binding or a foreign private alias.

    The underlying scope is the sealed container's own OpenScope implementation;
    the returned wrapper keeps holding it. Close runs the inner scope's bounded
    cleanup once and is idempotent; cancellation and closure of the context
    passed here are handled by the existing inner scope semantics.

    Errors: a nil context, a nil resolver, a typed-nil lifecycle resolver
    or any other resolver implementation (including the raw container or a
    delegating wrapper) is rejected; container failures (closed container,
    canceled context) surface unchanged from the inner OpenScope.

func Resolve[T any](ctx context.Context, resolver di.Resolver) (T, error)
    Resolve resolves T through the canonical module contract token and verifies
    the resolved value before returning it. Production hooks should prefer this
    error-returning façade over MustResolve.

func Service[T any]() di.Token
    Service returns the canonical exact-concrete-service token of T.


TYPES

type AddOption func(*addOptions)
    AddOption mutates constructor registration options.

func As(contract di.Token) AddOption
    As marks a constructor as an explicit cross-owner contribution to an
    interface contract exported by another module. The implementing module must
    directly depend on the contract owner; without As the constructor stays
    module-internal.

func Operation() AddOption
    Operation opts the constructor into per-operation lifetime; such services
    resolve only through scoped resolvers and must never be captured by a
    singleton, directly or through any Transient edge.

func Singleton() AddOption
    Singleton opts the constructor into shared singleton lifetime.

func Transient() AddOption
    Transient opts the constructor into transient lifetime (the default,
    kept explicit for readable registration sites).

type Base struct {
	Name               string
	Version            string
	RequiredScopeKinds []string
}
    Base is the ergonomic embeddable metadata descriptor. Embed it as a field so
    its ModuleMetadata method promotes to the module instance:

        type AuthModule struct {
            module.Base
        }

    All fields are optional: empty Name/Version keep the loader's derived
    defaults (full package path + type name, and Version "0.1.0").

func (b Base) ModuleMetadata() Metadata
    ModuleMetadata makes embedding Base satisfy MetadataProvider, returning a
    defensive copy so mutation cannot affect the module's declared metadata.

type Builder interface {
	di.Builder
	SetDefault(string, string) error
}

type Composition interface {
	// Services returns a registrar stamped with the owner. Revoke makes
	// previously handed handles unusable; a later call hands a fresh one.
	Services(owner string) (Services, error)
	// Provide registers a low-level provider with its exact token identity.
	Provide(owner string, p di.Provider) error
	// Replace swaps an existing low-level provider owned by this module,
	// preserving provider-owned token identity; reason is required.
	Replace(owner string, p di.Provider, reason string) error
	// Revoke invalidates previously handed Services handles for the owner.
	Revoke(owner string)
	// Seal validates the whole graph and returns the canonical di container.
	// Seal is one-shot, deterministic and runs no constructor eagerly except
	// the di eager singleton construction of the sealed container.
	Seal(ctx context.Context) (di.Container, error)
	// LifecycleResolver returns the post-seal restricted resolver of a
	// module: its own registrations plus direct dependencies' exported
	// tokens. Each Resolve runs inside one operation scope.
	LifecycleResolver(owner string) (di.Resolver, error)
	// ReplacementLog returns the provenance record of replacement
	// operations: constructor Replace, low-level Replace, binding and
	// contract implementation swaps, in registration order, each with its
	// recorded source module and reason.
	ReplacementLog() []string
}
    Composition is the trusted per-module constructor engine over a root plan.
    It owns its di registry; Seal returns the canonical di container after all
    contract, visibility and lifetime validation has run without executing any
    constructor.

func NewComposition(plan RootPlan, cleanupTimeout time.Duration) (Composition, error)
    NewComposition validates the root plan and builds the engine. The plan is
    the loader output (Plan.Ordered topological order keyed by name); the engine
    reads only names and direct dependency names from it.

type Configurer interface{ Configure(RootBuilder) error }

type Dependency struct {
	Name              string
	VersionConstraint string
}

type Depender interface {
	DependsOn() []Ref
}
    Depender is the optional interface a module instance implements to declare
    Type dependencies: func (m *XModule) DependsOn() []module.Ref.

type Metadata struct {
	Name               string
	Version            string
	RequiredScopeKinds []string
}
    Metadata is the optional base metadata a module declares through
    MetadataProvider. Empty fields fall back to defaults (derived qualified type
    name and Version "0.1.0", no required scope kinds), so one Go package can
    host several modules with distinct names.

type MetadataProvider interface {
	ModuleMetadata() Metadata
}
    MetadataProvider is the optional interface a module instance implements to
    override the derived base metadata.

type Module struct {
	Name               string
	Version            string
	DependsOn          []Dependency
	RequiredScopeKinds []string
	PreConfigure       func(Builder) error
	Configure          func(Builder) error
	PostConfigure      func(Builder) error
	Start              func(context.Context, Runtime) error
	Stop               func(context.Context, Runtime) error
}

type Plan struct {
	Ordered []Module
	Layers  [][]string
}
    Plan is a detached snapshot, not a mutable handle into a live registry.

type PostConfigurer interface{ PostConfigure(RootBuilder) error }

type PreConfigurer interface{ PreConfigure(RootBuilder) error }
    Optional root-module hooks; a module implements only what it needs and the
    runtime treats missing hooks as no-ops.

type Ref interface {
	Type() reflect.Type
	VersionConstraint() string
}
    Ref references another module by Go type with an optional version
    constraint. An empty constraint is unconstrained: the edge accepts the
    resolved module version, which is still validated as SemVer.

type Registry interface {
	Register(Module) error
	Plan() (Plan, error)
}

func NewRegistry() Registry
    NewRegistry creates an explicit, compile-time module registry.

type RootBuilder interface {
	SetDefault(key, value string) error
	Services() Services
	Provide(p di.Provider) error
	Replace(p di.Provider, reason string) error
}
    RootBuilder is the hook-facing registration view the root runtime hands
    to each module for the duration of one hook. The runtime owns window
    enforcement: after a hook returns it revokes the module's registrar, so any
    registrar stashed by the module is rejected by the engine on later use.

type RootPlan struct {
	// Plan stores the legacy Module metadata in stable topological order
	// (existing Registry.Plan); lifecycle hooks are nil because hook wiring
	// is owned by the root runtime.
	Plan Plan
	// Instances maps stable module name to actual instance: provided root
	// pointers are retained, Type dependencies are typed zero instances
	// created once per Type.
	Instances map[string]any
}
    RootPlan pairs the legacy module metadata snapshot with the actual module
    instances resolved from a root Type closure.

func LoadRoot(roots ...any) (RootPlan, error)
    LoadRoot builds the module graph from the transitive Type closure of
    the given root modules, deduplicating shared dependencies by Type. All
    graph validation (typed nils, invalid refs, unnamed struct types, cycles,
    name collisions, invalid versions and unsatisfied constraints) runs before
    any lifecycle hook or resource constructor: the loader executes no hooks and
    creates no resources beyond reflect.New zero instances.

type Runtime interface {
	Services() di.Resolver
	OpenScope(context.Context) (di.Scope, error)
	Config() config.Reader
}
    Runtime is a sealed service/config view. It cannot register providers.

type Services interface {
	// Add registers a constructor; the key is the exact returned type.
	// Lifetime defaults to Transient.
	Add(constructor any, opts ...AddOption) error
	// Replace re-registers a module-owned constructor producing the same
	// exact type; a non-empty reason is recorded.
	Replace(constructor any, reason string, opts ...AddOption) error
	// Export establishes this module as the single owner of a contract.
	Export(contract di.Token) error
	// Bind selects one implementation for a contract that has more than one
	// candidate; only the contract owner may bind.
	Bind(contract di.Token, impl any) error
	// ReplaceBinding swaps an existing binding owned by this module.
	ReplaceBinding(contract di.Token, impl any, reason string) error
	// ReplaceContract swaps this module's own explicit As contribution to a
	// contract it owns with a new constructor, preserving contract identity.
	ReplaceContract(contract di.Token, constructor any, reason string, opts ...AddOption) error
}
    Services registers constructors and contract declarations for one trusted
    module. Every operation is attributed to the owner the stamping host
    declared when handing out the registrar.

type Starter interface {
	Start(context.Context, Runtime) error
}

type Stopper interface {
	Stop(context.Context, Runtime) error
}

type Type[T any] struct {
	// Has unexported fields.
}
    Type references module T. T must be a named struct type: use Of[AuthModule],
    never Of[*AuthModule]; LoadRoot rejects pointer, interface and unnamed
    struct references.

