package authn // import "github.com/cymondez/pangolin-framework/security/authn"

Package authn verifies the concrete M1 credential adapters: the RS256 JWT
bearer validator and the deployment-selected service verifier. This file
keeps the published names working as explicit forwarding adapters over the
protocol-independent identity contract in security/identity; new authentication
modules implement identity.Verifier there without importing JWT parsing.

jwt.go holds the concrete RS256 JWT adapter: it verifies the M1 identity
slice against a trusted JWKS URL through a bounded key cache. Parsing details
stay here; the protocol-independent contract and trusted installation live in
security/identity.

service.go keeps the published service credential verifier and adapts it to the
identity contract: service credentials keep their distinct validated service
principal kind.

VARIABLES

var ErrUnauthenticated = identity.ErrUnauthenticated
    ErrUnauthenticated is the same fail-closed sentinel used by the identity
    pipeline; existing errors.Is callers keep working.


FUNCTIONS

func Identity(ctx context.Context) (scope.PrincipalRef, string, bool)
    Identity forwards to the trusted identity package storage. Resolvers keep
    receiving (principal, tenant, installed) exactly as before.


TYPES

type KeyPolicy struct {
	// CacheTTL trusts one fetched key set for this long. Within the TTL no
	// network fetch happens, so endpoint outages do not affect authentication.
	CacheTTL time.Duration
	// FetchCooldown is the minimum spacing between fetch attempts, measured
	// from each started attempt and consumed regardless of its outcome or
	// caller cancellation; during cooldown unknown-kid and expired-set
	// refreshes fail closed without network.
	FetchCooldown time.Duration
	// FetchTimeout bounds every single fetch through its own context
	// deadline, so source stalls stay bounded even when the HTTP client is
	// assembled with Timeout zero.
	FetchTimeout time.Duration
	// MaxKeys caps the number of usable keys kept from one document
	// (earliest document order wins; later entries, and any kid truncated
	// away, fail closed).
	MaxKeys int
	// MaxResponseBytes caps the accepted JWKS document size.
	MaxResponseBytes int
}
    KeyPolicy bounds one Validator's JWKS fetching, caching and key retention.
    Non-positive fields fall back to DefaultKeyPolicy; every bound exists so a
    hostile kid stream or broken key endpoint cannot consume unbounded work.

func DefaultKeyPolicy() KeyPolicy
    DefaultKeyPolicy returns the published bounded caching policy.

